A domain name and a URL are related but are not the same thing. Here is the difference

A domain name is just one part of a URL. A URL(Unifrom Resource Locator) is the full address used to reach a specific resource on 
the web.
For example:
https://github.com

https:// — the protocol
github.com — the domain name
So the domain name is github.com but the full URL is the entire string.

Here is an analogy that will help us understand better:
Imagine the internet were a city, the domain name is like a building's street address (e.g., 23 Budland Street),while
the URL is the full directions including which floor and room you're going to. Every URL contains a domain name, but a domain
name alone is not a full URL.
